#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on a Kali Linux system installation, enable snapd "
"and AppArmor services, and test it with hello-world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Kali Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:11
msgid ""
"Installing snap from a _live_ Kali Linux environment is not currently "
"supported. These instructions only work when Kali Linux is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:13
msgid ""
"From a Kali Linux installation, snap can be installed directly from the "
"command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:15
msgid ""
"sudo apt update\n"
"sudo apt install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:19
msgid ""
"If the *sudo* command isn't installed (usually because a root password was "
"provided at install time), you can install *snap* by first switching to the "
"*root* account:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:21
msgid ""
"su root\n"
"apt update\n"
"apt install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:27
msgid ""
"Additionally, enable and start both the snapd and the snapd.apparmor "
"services with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:29
msgid "systemctl enable --now snapd apparmor\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:33
msgid ""
"**Either log out and back in again, or restart your system, to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:35
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:37
msgid ""
"$ snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.3 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/kali.md:44
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Missing binaries <how-to-guides-fix-common-issues-index>` if snaps "
"are not added to the system path."
msgstr ""
